   "subject": "Re: dredge with occuMulti",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>For errors/bugs with dredge you&#39;ll have to ask the maintainer of the MuMIn package, I&#39;m not sure what the status of unmarked support is these days.</div><div><br></div><div>In general I would recommend against a dredging approach to model selection. This method can easily lead to spurious findings and overfitting especially if your dataset isn&#39;t that big. If you want to use model selection, I think it is better to create a set of candidate models specifically based on your hypotheses/predictions and test only those models.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Ken<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Monday, October 21, 2024 at 4:59:23 PM UTC-4 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kbrandon...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Is the dredge function from MuMIn no longer compatible with occu/occuMulti objects? I would like to dredge a global model to create unique models with all possible combinations of my covariates (64 combinations total; based on this <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/d0p_c9W_kRo/m/ZXM9sCDeAQAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/d0p_c9W_kRo/m/ZXM9sCDeAQAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448230278000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ff0m9sHJSWElivgLW4G-S\">approach</a>), but I am getting the error:   <span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(230,230,230)\">Error in getAllTerms.unmarkedFit(global.model, intercept = TRUE, data = eval(gmCall$data,  : \r\n  unknown &#39;unmarkedFit&#39; fit type: occuMulti</span><div><br></div><div>My code is a little complicated as I am applying it to a list of global models fit with penalized likelihood, but here is what I have so far:<br><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">#</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">1.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\"> Fit the global model\r\n#a. Define a </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(170,13,145)\">function</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">to</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">fit</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">the</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">global</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">model</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(92,38,153)\">(excluding species interactions)</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">\r\nset.seed(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">500</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">)\r\nstarting_values &lt;- rnorm(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">32</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">, mean = </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">, sd = </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">)                                 \r\nfit_global_model &lt;- function(umf_list){\r\n  model_list &lt;- list()\r\n  state_formulas &lt;- c(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(196,26,22);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">&quot;~Dist_urban + Above_MHW + Conn_vars_PC1 + Conn_vars_PC2 + Frag_vars_PC1 + Frag_vars_PC2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">)\r\n  state_formulas &lt;- c(rep(list(state_formulas), </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">4</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">))\r\n  </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(170,13,145);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">(i </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(170,13,145);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">in</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\"> seq_along(umf_list)){\r\n    model_list</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(196,26,22);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">[[i]]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\"> &lt;- occuMulti(\r\n      stateformulas = as.character(state_formulas),\r\n      detformulas = detformulas,\r\n      control = list(maxit=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(28,0,207);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">50000</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:12.24px;white-space:pre\">),\r\n      method = </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(196,26,22);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courie